\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Under prompt-chain recursion, $\Kempirical{=}2$ for web text at $\theta{=}0.60$ (8/9 configurations; stable across $\theta \in [0.575, 0.625]$), $\Kempirical{=}1$--$2$ for code, and $\Kempirical{=}3$ for arXiv; retrain-chain extends to $\Kempirical{=}7$ (Appendix~\ref{sec:extended_limitations}).
The domain ordering (arXiv $>$ C4 $\geq$ Code $>$ Wikipedia) is $\theta$-invariant.
A fine-tuned DeBERTa-v3-base ordinal classifier raises 1v2 $\auc$ to $0.678$ yet preserves $\Kempirical{=}2$ (2v3 CI upper ${<}\,\theta$), confirming a representation-independent boundary rather than a feature ceiling.
Future work includes retrain-chain $\Kempirical$ measurement, scale trends beyond 14B, and adaptive threshold selection.

